  "summary": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, recently married Durek Verrett, a self-identified sixth-generation shaman from California, in a unique wedding ceremony. The event, which took place in the village of Geiranger, attracted crowds despite its departure from standard royal traditions. The bride, who is fourth in the line of succession, wed the 49-year-old Verrett at a hotel near the Geiranger fjord, with notable attendees including various European royals and celebrities. Märtha Louise, who concluded her official royal responsibilities in 2022 to pursue business ventures with Verrett, has long eschewed convention, previously establishing a school focused on spiritual healing and communicating with angels. Verrett, known for his work with high-profile clients like Gwyneth Paltrow, identifies as an 'energy activator' and 'servant of God.'"
